        "content": "{\n  \"rule\": \"Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.\",\n  \"text\": \"The house came with a telephone mounted inside the pantry.\\n\\nNo dial. No cord.\\n\\nDuring the viewing, I asked whether it worked.\\n\\n“Only for emergencies,” the agent said, and shut the door.\\n\\nThree weeks after I moved in, it rang.\\n\\nI was chopping onions. I remember because I answered with the knife still in my hand.\\n\\n“Don't go upstairs,” a woman whispered.\\n\\n“Who is this?”\\n\\nAbove me, a floorboard creaked.\\n\\nI lived alone.\\n\\n“Put the knife down,” she said. “He'll take it from you.”\\n\\nI hung up and drove to my sister's.\\n\\nThe police found nothing. No broken windows, no footprints. They couldn't find the telephone either.\\n\\nWhen I returned, it was back.\\n\\nBeside it, someone had drawn a small pencil mark on the wall.\\n\\nOver the next month, it rang six times.\\n\\nDon't start the car.\\n\\nLeave the bathroom now.\\n\\nWhatever knocks tonight, let it finish.\\n\\nEach time, I obeyed.\\n\\nEach time, another mark appeared.\\n\\nOn the seventh call, the woman was crying.\\n\\n“I'm sorry,” she said. “I thought if I kept you alive long enough, someone would answer mine.”\\n\\nThe pantry door closed behind me.\\n\\nI pushed against it until my shoulder bruised. Through the wood, I heard someone enter the kitchen and begin chopping.\\n\\nThe receiver was still in my hand.\\n\\nIt had a dial now.\\n\\nI called my sister. A stranger answered.\\n\\nI called the police. The same stranger answered.\\n\\nThen I noticed writing beneath the pencil marks: a telephone number, scratched so deeply the plaster showed.\\n\\nI dialed.\\n\\nBeyond the pantry door, the chopping stopped.\\n\\nMy own voice answered.\\n\\n“Who is this?”\"\n}",
